+    // Destroy the renderer so the styles get removed from the DOM, otherwise
+    // they may leak back into the component together with the new ones.
+    this.rendererByCompId.get(componentId)?.destroy();
     this.rendererByCompId.delete(componentId);
   }
```

**What changed:** This is an internal bug fix in Angular's signal-query schematic (`packages/core/schematics/migrations/signal-queries-migration/migration.ts`), not an API change. Previously the migration counted queries that were *forcibly ignored* because of `--best-effort-mode` in its "incompatible" tally, so the summary printed after the run was wrong: e.g. a query such as `@ContentChildren('hello') options!: QueryList<HTMLDivElement>;` used via `this.options.changes.subscribe()` was migrated, yet the log still said `-> Migrated 0/1 queries. To see why 1 queries couldn't be migrated consider re-running with "--insert-todos" or "--best-effort-mode".` (). The fix adds a guard in `SignalQueriesMigration` that skips incrementing `incompatibleQueries++` when `this.config.bestEffortMode` is set and the field reason is `null` or not in the newly exported `nonIgnorableFieldIncompatibilities` list, so best-effort runs now report `-> Migrated 2/2 queries.` / `-> Migrated 2/2 inputs.` (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/eb2fcd1896e0b834b86fe79e8d806bdab24aabcc). The same corrected counting applies to the signal-input migration (`signal-input-migration`) per the added specs (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/eb2fcd1896e0b834b86fe79e8d806bdab24aabcc.patch). Shipped as part of PR #59463 "Signal migration follow-ups" (https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/59463).

**Affects:** Only the console statistics printed by `ng g @angular/core:signals --migrations=queries` (and the signal-input migration) when `--best-effort-mode` is used. No application code, template, dependency or configuration is affected; generated code output is unchanged.

**Action:** none — nothing to change in applications. Teams that previously read the misleading "Migrated 0/N queries" output when running with `--best-effort-mode` should re-verify their migration progress reports; the numbers are now accurate.

**Before/after:**
```ts
