**What changed:** In v20, `afterRender`/`afterNextRender` calls made with a component/directive (i.e. view) `Injector` are no longer registered eagerly: registration is deferred until the associated view has been rendered for the first time, so the callback can no longer fire "too early" (before the view it belongs to exists in the DOM) — "For `afterRender`/`afterNextRender` calls associated with a particular view, ensure that they are not registered until after the first time the view is rendered." (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/9870b643bff46f089a3f0a30514fb7e062a66d56, https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/58250). Implementation-wise, v20's `afterEveryRenderImpl` resolves `const viewContext = injector.get(ViewContext, null, {optional: true})` and passes `viewContext?.view` into the new `AfterRenderSequence` constructor so the sequence is tied to that view (packages/core/src/render3/after_render/hooks.ts at tag 20.0.0), whereas in 19.0 `afterRenderImpl` created the sequence with no view (`new AfterRenderSequence(manager.impl, getHooks(...), once, destroyRef)`) and registered it immediately (packages/core/src/render3/after_render/hooks.ts at tag 19.0.0). In the same PR, the sibling commit a5fc962094 "fix(core): Don't run effects in check no changes pass" (#58250) stopped effects from running during `provideCheckNoChangesConfig`/check-no-changes passes.

**Affects:** Applications that call `afterRender` (renamed `afterEveryRender` in v20) or `afterNextRender` from a component/directive injection context (constructor, field initializer, or with `options.injector` pointing at a node/element injector), and code that asserted on the exact render cycle in which such callbacks ran; also code relying on effects running during check-no-changes debug passes.

**Action:** required: re-verify timing-sensitive `afterNextRender`/`afterEveryRender` callbacks registered in component constructors — DOM measurements, third-party library initialization, focus management and scroll restoration — for ordering/execution-count changes now that registration waits for the view's first render; no dependency or API change is needed in application code for this behavior fix.

**Before/after:**
```typescript
// 19.0 (packages/core/src/render3/after_render/hooks.ts)
const sequence = new AfterRenderSequence(
  manager.impl,
  getHooks(callbackOrSpec, hooks),
  once,
  destroyRef,
);
manager.impl.register(sequence);

// 20.0
const viewContext = injector.get(ViewContext, null, {optional: true});
const sequence = new AfterRenderSequence(
  manager.impl,
  getHooks(callbackOrSpec),
  viewContext?.view,
  once,
  destroyRef,
  tracing?.snapshot(null),
);
manager.impl.register(sequence);
```

**What changed:** In Angular 20, effects are no longer executed during the "check no changes" change detection pass. Specifically, `runEffectsInView(lView)` is now conditionally guarded by `!isInCheckNoChangesPass` (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/a5fc9620948c59da2146d46d27de388839b93254). Additionally, `afterRender` and `afterNextRender` hooks associated with a specific view are deferred until after that view's first render, rather than being registered immediately (https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/58250).

**Affects:** Applications using `effect()` in components that are checked with `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` during the debug/no-changes pass, or those relying on `afterRender`/`afterNextRender` hooks being registered before the view's first render (e.g., in dynamic component creation or defer blocks).

**Action:** required: Re-verify that side-effects in `effect()` are not expected to run during check-no-changes passes. Re-verify the timing of `afterRender` and `afterNextRender` callbacks; ensure logic depending on hook registration prior to initial render is adjusted to occur post-render.

**Before/after:**
```typescript
// Before (Angular 19): Effects ran in checkNoChanges
function detectChangesInView(lView: LView, mode: ChangeDetectionMode) {
  // ...
  } else if (flags & LViewFlags.HasChildViewsToRefresh) {
    runEffectsInView(lView); // Always ran
    // ...
  }
}

// After (Angular 20): Effects skipped in checkNoChanges
function detectChangesInView(lView: LView, mode: ChangeDetectionMode) {
  // ...
  } else if (flags & LViewFlags.HasChildViewsToRefresh) {
    if (!isInCheckNoChangesPass) { // New check
      runEffectsInView(lView);
    }
    // ...
  }
}
```

