**What changed:** `AsyncAnimationRendererFactory` (in `@angular/platform-browser/animations/async`, used via `provideAnimationsAsync()`) previously resolved `ChangeDetectionScheduler` eagerly in its constructor (`inject(ChangeDetectionScheduler, {optional: true})`). Since the CDK overlay began depending on `Renderer2Factory` (angular/components#30179) and `Overlay` (via `MatSnackbar`, often used in error handlers) can be injected during app initialization, this could produce a `Circular dependency in DI detected for ChangeDetectionScheduler` runtime error (angular/angular#59255). The fix injects `Injector` instead and resolves the scheduler lazily when the async animations chunk loads: `this.scheduler ??= this.injector.get(ChangeDetectionScheduler, null, {optional: true});` before `this.scheduler?.notify(NotificationSource.AsyncAnimationsLoaded);` (https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/59256, https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/8c5db3cfb75700dd64f4c8c073554c7086835950, https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/59256/files)

**Affects:** Applications using `provideAnimationsAsync()` together with `@angular/cdk`/`@angular/material` ≥19.0.4 where `Overlay`/`MatSnackBar` (typically via an `ErrorHandler`) is injected during app initialization. This is purely an internal bug fix; no public API changed.

**Action:** none — the circular DI error is fixed in 20.0.0. Applications that had hit the regression should simply re-verify that apps using `provideAnimationsAsync()` with an `ErrorHandler` injecting `MatSnackBar`/`Overlay` boot without `R3Injector` cyclic-dependency errors.

