**What changed:** During Hot Module Replacement, Angular's internal `ɵɵreplaceMetadata` function previously swapped out the whole component definition object (e.g. `MyComp.ɵcmp = newDef`). For module-based (non-standalone) components where the AoT compiler emits a `setComponentScope` call from the *NgModule's* file (e.g. due to circular dependencies), that call is not part of the component's HMR replacement function, so the component's dependencies (`directiveDefs`, `pipeDefs`) were cleared on replacement — causing `NgFor`/`AsyncPipe` errors when editing a module-declared component's template/style (issue #59639). The fix in `packages/core/src/render3/hmr.ts` now merges the new definition into the existing one via `mergeWithExistingDefinition`, copying properties with `Object.assign(currentDef, newDef, {...})` while preserving the original `directiveDefs`, `pipeDefs` and `setInput` from a clone of the old def, then re-assigns it via `NG_COMP_DEF` (`(type as any)[NG_COMP_DEF] = newDef`) (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/d7575c201cfd61010952b3a633eec03e32f58220.patch). This also prevents stale definition references held by other defs' `directiveDefs`/`pipeDefs`. Shipped in Angular 20.0.0 (https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/59644).

**Affects:** Only affects dev-time behavior of applications using HMR (`ng serve --hmr`) with components declared in NgModules (non-standalone), particularly when template/style edits previously broke `NgFor`/`AsyncPipe` or other scoped dependencies. No application source code, configuration, or public API is involved — the change is entirely inside `@angular/core`'s HMR implementation.

**Action:** none

**Before/after:**
```ts
// packages/core/src/render3/hmr.ts (Angular 20.0.0) — mergeWithExistingDefinition
const replacement = Object.assign(currentDef, newDef, {
  // We need to keep the existing directive and pipe defs, because they can get patched on
  // by a call to `setComponentScope` from a module file.
  directiveDefs: clone.directiveDefs,
  pipeDefs: clone.pipeDefs,

  // Preserve the old `setInput` function, because it has some state.
  setInput: clone.setInput,
});
```

**What changed:** In development mode (`ngDevMode`), the framework checks for component ID collisions and emits the `NG0912` warning "Component ID generation collision detected". Previously this check ran even under server-side rendering, but during SSR the same component instance cannot be guaranteed between requests, so it falsely warned for components being replaced (checking `componentDef.type` was insufficient). The check in `getComponentId` (`packages/core/src/render3/definition.ts`) is now additionally gated on `ngServerMode`, skipping the warning when `typeof ngServerMode === 'undefined' || !ngServerMode` is false, i.e. the warning is disabled during SSR (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/26f6d4c485b566d7bc127c78cc163c376d0fe6b5, https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/59625). The collision warning remains enabled in the browser because it is primarily useful there (https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/59625, https://github.com/angular/angular-cli/issues/29408).

**Affects:** Applications using SSR in development mode that previously saw spurious `NG0912` warnings (e.g. during dev-server rebuilds); no application code, configuration, or dependencies are affected.

**Action:** none

**Before/after:**
```typescript
// packages/core/src/render3/definition.ts — getComponentId()

// Before
if (typeof ngDevMode === 'undefined' || ngDevMode) {
  if (GENERATED_COMP_IDS.has(compId)) {
    ...
  }
}

// After
if (
  (typeof ngDevMode === 'undefined' || ngDevMode) &&
  (typeof ngServerMode === 'undefined' || !ngServerMode)
) {
  if (GENERATED_COMP_IDS.has(compId)) {
    ...
  }
}
```

**What changed:** The `AsyncAnimationRendererFactory` (in `packages/platform-browser/animations/async/src/async_animation_renderer.ts`) gained a `componentReplaced(componentId: string)` method that calls `this._engine?.flush()` and forwards the call to the delegated renderer factory (`(this.delegate as {componentReplaced?: (id: string) => void}).componentReplaced?.(componentId)`) (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/b2b3816cb1c5c573dc9368f05fd2971671d7159f). Previously only the synchronous animations renderer had this logic (added in PR #59393, where "an animation-specific renderer factory ... wraps the base DOM one and was preventing the cache from being cleared" — https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/59393); the async renderer introduced by `provideAnimationsAsync()` did not, so its style cache was never cleared during Hot Module Replacement (HMR) and component style edits (inline or file-based styles) were not applied in dev mode — reported for module-based, module+standalone, and fully standalone apps (https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/59640). The fix is a patch-level bug fix shipped as part of PR #59644, a bundle of HMR-related fixes (https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/59644).

**Affects:** Applications using `provideAnimationsAsync()` from `@angular/platform-browser/animations/async` together with HMR (`ng serve --hmr`); no production or build-time behaviour changes.

**Action:** none — the fix is internal to `@angular/platform-browser`; just re-verify that style edits are picked up during `ng serve --hmr` in dev after upgrading.

**Before/after:**
```ts
// packages/platform-browser/animations/async/src/async_animation_renderer.ts (new in v20)
/**
 * Used during HMR to clear any cached data about a component.
 * @param componentId ID of the component that is being replaced.
 */
protected componentReplaced(componentId: string) {
  // Flush the engine since the renderer destruction waits for animations to be done.
  this._engine?.flush();
  (this.delegate as {componentReplaced?: (id: string) => void}).componentReplaced?.(componentId);
}
```

