**What changed:** `createCustomElement()` from `@angular/elements` previously skipped signal-based inputs (`input()`/`input.required()`) when re-applying pre-existing values that were set as properties on the custom element before upgrade/insertion. The constructor loop was `inputs.forEach(({propName, transform, isSignal}) => { if (!this.hasOwnProperty(propName) || isSignal) { return; } ... })`; Angular 20 removed the `isSignal` exclusion so the check is now only `if (!this.hasOwnProperty(propName))`, and the value is re-applied via `strategy.setInputValue(propName, value, transform)` (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/44180645992f7d9018ccb2d7663530b3cffde36b, confirmed in the v20.0.x source https://raw.githubusercontent.com/angular/angular/20.0.x/packages/elements/src/create-custom-element.ts). This fixes issue #59757, where signal inputs on an Angular custom element were initialized correctly on client-side navigation but reverted to their defaults on a direct page load/refresh, while `@Input()` worked (https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/59757).

**Affects:** Applications that wrap components in `createCustomElement()` and set values on the element as properties before upgrade/insertion into the DOM (e.g. via the generated `WithProperties<P>` accessors or `Object.assign` on a pre-upgrade element), where the component uses `input()`/`input.required()` signal inputs.

**Action:** none — behavior-only bug fix; re-verify that pre-set property values for signal-based inputs now reach the component (attributes/`attributeChangedCallback` handling of signal inputs was unchanged).

**Before/after:**
```typescript
// Angular 19 (create-custom-element.ts)
inputs.forEach(({propName, transform, isSignal}) => {
  if (!this.hasOwnProperty(propName) || isSignal) {
    // No pre-existing value for `propName`, or a signal input.
    return;
  }
  // Delete the property from the instance and re-apply it through the strategy.
  ...
});

// Angular 20
inputs.forEach(({propName, transform}) => {
  if (!this.hasOwnProperty(propName)) {
    // No pre-existing value for `propName`.
    return;
  }
  // Delete the property from the DOM node and re-apply it through the strategy.
  ...
});
```

