**What changed:** In `packages/core/src/render3/hmr.ts`, when a callback throws during Hot Module Replacement (component HMR / `angular:invalidate` flow), Angular previously sent only the error's `message` over the dev-server WebSocket channel; now it also appends the error's `stack`. The payload to `importMeta?.hot?.send?.('angular:invalidate', {id, message: toLog, error: true})` now carries `error.message + '\n' + error.stack` instead of just `message`, so the CLI dev server and browser console show a full stack trace for HMR failures (e.g. `Component update failed: Cannot read properties of undefined` — angular-cli#29695). The error is still rethrown so the page reloads if it is not invalidated. (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/c611c8d212b0134365954726c2fd6c98c28e5424, https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/60067)

