**What changed:** `resource()` now supports streaming response data via a new `stream` option used instead of `loader`. The `stream` function returns `Promise<Signal<{value: T}|{error: unknown}>>`; once resolved, the resource continuously delivers updates (values or errors) from that signal over time (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/bc2ad7bfd37a61992b550943de5da0eab2eec98b). The `rxResource()` factory now also uses a `stream` property (renamed from `loader`) and by default behaves as a streaming resource, delivering multiple values from its Observable (https://dev.to/railsstudent/resource-api-changes-in-angular-20-streaming-data-in-rxresource-pg4).

**Affects:** Applications calling `rxResource()` and passing the `loader` property; or migrating to the new `stream` option of `resource()`.

**Action:** required: rename the `loader` property to `stream` when defining a resource with `rxResource()` or a streaming `resource()`.

