**What changed:** In v20 the experimental `provideExperimentalCheckNoChangesForDebug` (from `@angular/core`) was renamed to `provideCheckNoChangesConfig`, promoted to developer preview, and its `exhaustive` behavior now applies to _all_ `checkNoChanges` runs rather than a subset. Previously the "no expressions changed" verification skipped views (notably `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` components not marked for check); now, with `exhaustive` enabled, all views attached to `ApplicationRef` and their descendants are treated as `ChangeDetectionStrategy.Eager`/`Default` and checked for changes (excluding subtrees detached via `ChangeDetectorRef.detach()`), surfacing errors previously hidden by `OnPush` (https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/60906/files). The `useNgZoneOnStable` option is removed (not generally more useful than `interval`, which periodically runs `checkNoChanges` on application views) (https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/60906/files). The new symbol is exported from `@angular/core` as `provideCheckNoChangesConfig` (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/angular/angular/20.0.x/packages/core/src/core.ts). Signature: `function provideCheckNoChangesConfig(options: { exhaustive: false; }): EnvironmentProviders` (https://angular.dev/api/core/provideCheckNoChangesConfig).

**Affects:** Only applications that called `provideExperimentalCheckNoChangesForDebug` (a debug/dev-mode-only provider) in their bootstrap providers, especially those relying on the `useNgZoneOnStable` option; the stricter `exhaustive` behavior can surface pre-existing `ExpressionChangedAfterItHasBeenCheckedError`s from `OnPush` components.

**Action:** required: rename the imported/called function `provideExperimentalCheckNoChangesForDebug` to `provideCheckNoChangesConfig` and drop the removed `useNgZoneOnStable` option (use `interval` instead); re-verify dev-mode change-detection runs for new `ExpressionChangedAfterItHasBeenCheckedError`s from `OnPush` components once the exhaustive check covers all runs.

