  el = inject(ElementRef, InjectFlags.Optional | InjectFlags.Host | InjectFlags.SkipSelf);
}

// After (Angular 20)
import { inject, ElementRef } from '@angular/core';

@Directive()
export class Dir {
  el = inject(ElementRef, { optional: true, host: true, skipSelf: true });
}
```

**What changed:** In Angular 20, the `InjectFlags` enum is removed from the public API and `EnvironmentInjector.get` no longer accepts `InjectFlags` as an argument (previously `get(token, flags?)`); the same removal applies to `inject`, `Injector.get`, `TestBed.get`, and `TestBed.inject` (https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/60318). Bitwise flags (e.g. `InjectFlags.Optional`, `InjectFlags.Host`, `InjectFlags.SkipSelf`) were replaced by an options-object form such as `{ optional: true, host: true, skipSelf: true }`, an API introduced in v14.1 (https://angular.love/angular-20-whats-new).

**Affects:** Applications or libraries that call `EnvironmentInjector.get` (or the other DI APIs) with an `InjectFlags` argument, or that import `InjectFlags` from `@angular/core`.

**Action:** required: remove `InjectFlags` from `@angular/core` imports and rewrite each call to pass the options object instead of the bitwise flags, e.g. `{ optional: true, host: true, skipSelf: true }`. A migration schematic performs this automatically during `ng update` (https://angular.love/angular-20-whats-new). Also verify any third-party libraries still passing `InjectFlags`, as those will fail to compile/run (https://angular.love/angular-20-whats-new).

**Before/after:**
```typescript
import { inject, InjectFlags, Directive, ElementRef } from '@angular/core';
@Directive()
export class Dir {
  el = inject(ElementRef, InjectFlags.Optional | InjectFlags.Host | InjectFlags.SkipSelf);
}
```
→
```typescript
el = inject(ElementRef, { optional: true, host: true, skipSelf: true });
```

