**What changed:** In Angular v20 the `InjectFlags` enum was removed from the public API and all public injection signatures that previously accepted an `InjectFlags` argument no longer do so, including `TestBed.inject`. This is part of the v20 breaking change set that also removes `inject`, `Injector.get`, `EnvironmentInjector.get`, and `TestBed.get` flag parameters (https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/60318). The removed flags (deprecated since v14.1) are replaced by the options-object form of the DI APIs; an automated migration from `InjectFlags` to the object literal ships with the update (https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/60318).

